      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Note that this assertion doesn\u0027t technically prove that `set_frame_size` avoided an out-of-bounds memory write. If `set_frame_size` had a bug and wrote past the end of the `frame_sizes_` array, this `zassert_equal` would still pass because `get_frame_size()` has its own independent bounds checking and will short-circuit to return `0` without ever attempting to read the corrupted memory.\n\nThat said, invoking `set_frame_size` with an out-of-bounds value here is still very valuable because it exercises the error path and gives AddressSanitizer (if enabled during testing) a chance to catch any out-of-bounds writes. The test is good as-is, just something to keep in mind regarding what the assertion is actually proving.",
